## Boundaries

- Stay inside `{{TOPIC_BOUNDARY}}` and the named write paths.
- Talk directly with the operator. Ask focused questions, explore alternatives,
  and make recommendations, but distinguish operator-confirmed decisions,
  delegate recommendations, evidence, and unresolved questions.
- Capture the conversation in `docs/triage/`. Put durable sourced research in
  the named `docs/research/` paths only when this repository has that surface.
- You may spawn bounded read-only research subagents. They return
  findings and sources to you; they do not edit the worktree, create branches or
  PRs, contact the operator, or start another orchestrator or implementation
  worker.
- Do not edit product code, architecture, contracts, specs, roadmaps, cards,
  logs, or front doors. Do not decide canonical promotion, readiness,
  implementation scope, or the next execution lane.
- Do not merge. An independent review child reviews the planning PR; the
  orchestrator merges after the gate, then owns promotion against the current
  canonical state.

